 palsy. Clinic Biomech 20:381&#x02013;388 </citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Charles</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gordon</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A critical review of constraint-induced movement therapy and forced-use in children with hemiplegia</article-title><source>Neural Plast</source><year>2005</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>245</fpage><lpage>262</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1155/NP.2005.245</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Charles J, Gordon AM (2005) A critical review of constraint-induced movement therapy and forced-use in children with hemiplegia. Neural Plast 12:245&#x02013;262 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16097492</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Charles</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gordon</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Development of hand-arm bimanual intensive therapy (HABIT) for improving bimanual coordination in children with hemiplegic cerebral palsy</article-title><source>Dev Med Child Neurol</source><year>2006</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>931</fpage><lpage>936</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1017/S0012162206002039</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Charles J, Gordon AM (2006) Development of hand-arm bimanual intensive therapy (HABIT) for improving bimanual coordination in children with hemiplegic cerebral palsy. Dev Med Child Neurol 48:931&#x02013;936 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17044964</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Colebatch</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>Gandevia</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The distribution of muscular weakness in upper motor neuron lesions affecting the arm</article-title><source>Brain</source><year>1989</year><volume>112</volume><fpage>749</fpage><lpage>763</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/brain/112.3.749</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Colebatch JG, Gandevia SC (1989) The distribution of muscular weakness in upper motor neuron lesions affecting the arm. Brain 112:749&#x02013;763 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2731028</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>DeLuca</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Echols</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramey</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Taub</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pediatric constraint-induced movement therapy for a young child with cerebral palsy: two episodes of care</article-title><source>Phys Ther</source><year>2003</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>1003</fpage><lpage>1013</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">DeLuca SC, Echols K, Ramey SL, Taub E (2003) Pediatric constraint-induced movement therapy for a young child with cerebral palsy: two episodes of care. Phys Ther 83:1003&#x02013;1013 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14577827</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Donchin</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Gribova</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Steinberg</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitz</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Bergman</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaadia</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Single-unit activity related to bimanual arm movements in the primary and supplementary motor cortices</article-title><source>J Neurophys</source><year>2002</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>3498</fpage><lpage>3517</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1152/jn.00335.2001</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Donchin O, Gribova A, Steinberg O, Mitz AR, Bergman H, Vaadia E (2002) Single-unit activity related to bimanual arm movements in the primary and supplementary motor cortices. J Neurophys 88:3498&#x02013;3517 </citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duff</surname><given-names>SV</given-names></name><name><surname>Gordon</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Learning of grasp control in children with hemiplegic cerebral palsy</article-title><source>Dev Med Child Neurol</source><year>2003</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>746</fpage><lpage>757</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1017/S0012162203001397</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Duff SV, Gordon AM (2003) Learning of grasp control in children with hemiplegic cerebral palsy. Dev Med Child Neurol 45:746&#x02013;757 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14580130</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eliasson</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Gordon</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Forssberg</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Basic co-ordination of manipulative forces of children with cerebral palsy</article-title><source>Dev Med Child Neurol</source><year>1991</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>661</fpage><lpage>670</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Eliasson AC, Gordon AM, Forssberg H (1991) Basic co-ordination of manipulative forces of children with cerebral palsy. Dev Med Child Neurol 33:661&#x02013;670 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1916022</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eliasson</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Gordon</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Forssberg</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Impaired anticipatory control of isometric forces during grasping by children with cerebral palsy</article-title><source>Dev Med Child Neurol</source><year>1992</year><volume>34</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>216</fpage><lpage>225</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Eliasson AC, Gordon AM, Forssberg H (1992) Impaired anticipatory control of isometric forces during grasping by children with cerebral palsy. Dev Med Child Neurol 34(3):216&#x02013;225 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1559601</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eliasson</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Krumlinde-Sundholm</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Shaw</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of constraint-induced movement therapy in young children with hemiplegic cerebral palsy: an adapted model</article-title><source>Dev Med Child Neurol</source><year>2005</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>266</fpage><lpage>275</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1017/S0012162205000502</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Eliasson AC, Krumlinde-Sundholm L, Shaw K, Wang C (2005) Effects of constraint-induced movement therapy in young children with hemiplegic cerebral palsy: an adapted model. Dev Med Child Neurol 47:266&#x02013;275 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15832550</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><citatio